  "rule": "post-change action frequency must vary with true tau_c. Judged on the REALISED ACTION contrast f(tau_c=20) - f(tau_c=1) with replicate-level uncertainty, not on a floor.",
  "estimator_choices": {
    "all_replicates": "fixed-horizon statistics use every replicate. run_batch keeps simulating a run after it alarms, so its actions to any horizon exist; the earlier survivor-only version compared 13 surviving tau_c=20 runs against 57 tau_c=1 runs, i.e. different subpopulations.",
    "simultaneous_coverage": "four horizons were inspected, so per-horizon 95 % intervals are Bonferroni-widened to 98.75 %. Reporting the horizon that happens to resolve would be selection on the outcome.",
    "why_not_lifetime": "the lifetime contrast is SURVIVAL-CONFOUNDED: it describes the trajectories actually accumulated before alarm, which is a real property of them, but the two tau_c conditions contribute radically different observation lengths -- 7523 shots against 1358 for greedy/pilot -- so it cannot establish adaptation."
